Package: DenMark
Type: Package
Title: Cell-Density Correlated Genes from Spatial Transcriptomics
Version: 0.9.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Mingchi", "Xu", role = "aut"),
    person(c("Alexandra", "M."), "Schmidt", role = "aut"),
    person("Qihuang", "Zhang", email = "qihuang.zhang@mcgill.ca",
           role = c("aut", "cre"), comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0003-1455-2159"))
  )
Description: Quantifies the dependence between local cell density and gene
    expression in single-cell resolution spatial transcriptomics data, such as
    data from the Xenium and MERFISH platforms. Cell locations form a point
    pattern and gene counts are its marks. After aggregation on a regular
    grid, cell counts and summed expression follow Poisson models driven by
    two coregionalized latent Gaussian fields with Matern covariance,
    approximated by Hilbert space basis functions; the correlation between
    the two fields measures the density-expression dependence. Models are
    fitted with 'Stan' through 'cmdstanr'. Functions cover the tissue
    boundary (an alpha shape of the cells), gridding, model fitting,
    posterior summaries, latent-field decomposition, spatial correlation
    ranges, and gene scans that call density-correlated genes.
